    <!-- ============================ CLERK-OF-THE-WORKS ============================ -->
    <section class="section service-details advisory-clerk" id="clerk">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="section-head center" data-reveal>
          <span class="eyebrow">Service Area Two</span>
          <h2 data-reveal-words>Clerk of the Works</h2>
          <hr class="rule">
        </div>
        <p class="advisory-lede" data-reveal data-delay="1">Clerk of the Works oversight documents site progress, observes work against the drawings and specifications, and reports issues to the owner. Depending on the agreed scope, this includes:</p>

        <article class="svc-card clerk-card" data-reveal data-delay="2">
          <ul class="adu-points cols-2">
            <li>Project-records maintenance, including contractor certificates of insurance</li>
            <li>Process &amp; quality control</li>
            <li>Review of the general contractor's record-keeping</li>
            <li>Monitoring the construction schedule &amp; identifying potential delays</li>
            <li>Construction-cost monitoring</li>
            <li>Safety-program review</li>
            <li>Investigation of &amp; recommendations on proposed change orders</li>
            <li>Assistance negotiating the cost of proposed change orders</li>
            <li>Review of contractor progress-payment requests</li>
            <li>Shop-drawing &amp; submittal review (samples and other submittals)</li>
            <li>Monthly progress-report submission</li>
          </ul>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============================ CONSTRUCTION ADVISORY ============================ -->
    <section class="section service-details advisory-ca" id="construction-advisory">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="section-head center" data-reveal>
          <span class="eyebrow">Service Area Three</span>
          <h2 data-reveal-words>Construction Advisory</h2>
          <hr class="rule">
        </div>
        <p class="advisory-lede" data-reveal data-delay="1">We don't manage the job site. We protect the investment. While the Owner's Representative drives day-to-day project execution and the Lender monitors budget compliance, when we act as a Construction Advisor, we provide high-level risk management and specialized technical foresight. Think of us as the strategic advisor for the project, ensuring both alignment and protection across all stakeholders.</p>
        <p class="advisory-lede" data-reveal data-delay="2">Your Owner's Rep is in the trenches every day making sure contractor submittals are in and the schedule moves forward. We serve as your executive sounding board: reviewing high-stakes contract terms, auditing schedule logic before critical delays happen, and giving you objective, peer-level guidance when tough decisions arise.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section service-details">
      <div class="container">
        <h2>Define the oversight your project needs</h2>
        <p class="advisory-lede">For a project  or the South Shore, share the town, project stage, your role and the decisions you need help with. A first conversation can clarify whether owner’s representation, Clerk of the Works support or a focused advisory scope is appropriate.</p>
        <p class="advisory-lede">Before engagement, confirm relevant experience, availability, reporting frequency, authority and deliverables. Design, permitting and contractor responsibilities should be explicit in the agreed scope.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    
